# Line-ending policy for reproducible release artifacts.
#
# `release-manifest.json` records content hashes (dependency files, deployable
# artifacts and an aggregate source-tree hash) as the identity of a release
# archive. Without a policy, `core.autocrlf=true` makes `git checkout` and
# `git archive` rewrite line endings on Windows only, so the same commit would
# produce DIFFERENT artifact hashes on Windows and Linux, and an exported ZIP
# could not be checked against the repository's committed blobs.
#
# Pin every text file to LF in the repository and in the worktree so the
# committed blob, a fresh working copy and the exported archive are
# byte-identical on every platform. `scripts/make_release_archive.py` also
# forces `core.autocrlf=false -c core.eol=lf` so the archive guarantee does not
# depend on a host's git configuration.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets are never converted and never diffed as text.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.zip  binary
*.xlsx binary
*.xlsm binary
*.xls  binary
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf  binary
*.exe  binary
